{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The only observed data variable scored by a sampling statement is the top-level variable `y`, which is observed exactly once with the built-in distribution `normal`. Context inputs `N`, `J`, and `county` are not protected because they are used only as sizes/indices. Each parameter has exactly one built-in prior before later model-block use.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  int<lower=1> J; // number of counties
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  real mu_a;
  real<lower=0> sigma_a;
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
  vector<offset=mu_a, multiplier=sigma_a>[J] a; // county intercepts
}
model {
  mu_a ~ std_normal();
  sigma_a ~ cauchy(0, 2.5);
  sigma_y ~ cauchy(0, 2.5);
  a ~ normal(mu_a, sigma_a);
  y ~ normal(a[county], sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":1,"N":5,"county":[1,1,1,1,1],"y":[2.0,5.0,5.0,3.0,3.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
